  "description": "Formatting showcase: custom formats for every precision (and intercalary ones) using every token and modifier, plus non-default display options (circa 'ca. ', digit group '.', scientific notation from 9 digits with 3 significant digits, range separator ' to '). Base unit second; levels minute (60 s) → hour → day → month → year. A year has 121 days: Frostfall (abbr Fro) and Thawing (30 days), the intercalary one-day month Midyear's Day (excluded from the week), then two unnamed 30-day months (3 and 4). A 5-day named week and an unnamed 3-day market cycle start on 1 Frostfall 1. Eras BF (backward, suffix) and AF (forward from 1 Frostfall 1, prefix). A moon overlay with a 10-day period is new at 1 Frostfall 1, which is aligned with t = 10,454,400,000 so that year −999 starts at t = 0.",
